-- title:
--   Residue field of a DVR in ℚ(ζₚ) above p is generated by ℤ
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime number and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, i.e. $L$ is generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by a primitive $p$-th root of unity; thus $L$ is a copy of $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$. Let $A$ be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring, equipped with an algebra structure over which $L$ is the fraction field of $A$, and assume that the image of $p$ in $A$ lies in the maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}_A$ of the local ring $A$. The conclusion is that the ring homomorphism $\mathbb{Z} \to A/\mathfrak{m}_A$, namely the canonical map of $\mathbb{Z}$ into the residue field of $A$, is surjective as a function: every residue class in $A/\mathfrak{m}_A$ is the class of a rational integer. Equivalently, $A$ has residue degree $1$ over $p$, so that its residue field is $\mathbb{F}_p$ (the identification with $\mathbb{Z}/p$ itself requires knowing in addition the characteristic of the residue field).
--
--   This records the residue-degree-one half of the classical fact that $p$ is totally ramified in $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$, in the form needed for local computations at a place above $p$: every residue of such a discrete valuation ring comes from $\mathbb{Z}$, because $\zeta_p \equiv 1$ modulo the maximal ideal. It is used downstream to identify Frobenius and residue fields at $p$ for cyclotomic local rings, and in the analysis of inertia on integral models of the modular curves $X_1(p)$, $X_0(p)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsCyclotomicExtension_Rat_surjective_algebraMap_int_residueField_of_isDiscreteValuationRing.lean

